# Fault (writer 7's brief): L §8.2 pinned: "A pin given by an expression prints its value, pinned: <pin> = v, and
# with it the register of what the expression read". old_y reads y as if {law old_last_day}, old_last_day = 2025-06-30:
# pinned: law old_last_day = 2025-06-30 (refcore printed pinned: law 2025-06-30); a literal pin prints as written (q2).
# y's 2025 row gives 1 (L5_11_asif_law.test).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input rate: int
input old_last_day: date

def y: int at reader
  rule base = rate

def old_y: int = y as if {law old_last_day}

version v0
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  old_last_day = 2025-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 1

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  replace rate = 2

ask q1: old_y
ask q2: y as if {law 2025-06-30}
=== expect
q1: 1
  pinned: law old_last_day = 2025-06-30
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: 1
  pinned: law 2025-06-30
  cut 2026-12-31
